testExtractedStatements;req;r;db;con;count;extracted;st;stmt;res;msg
⍝ Isolated tests for extracted statements API.

:If 0=⎕NC'null'
    init 'lib/'
:EndIf

req←{0::⍺,' - FAILED: ',⎕DMX.Message ⋄ ⍵:⍺,' - OK' ⋄ ⍺,' - FAILED'}
r←⊂'Test Extracted Statements API'

db←open ':memory:'
con←connect db

⍝ Success path: two statements in one SQL string.
(count extracted)←extractStatements(con 'SELECT 1 AS a; SELECT 2 AS b')
r,←⊂'extract_statements count is 2' req 2=count
r,←⊂'extract_statements returned handle' req extracted≠0

:If extracted≠0
    (st stmt)←prepareExtractedStatement(con extracted 0)
    r,←⊂'prepare extracted statement[0] success' req (DuckDBSuccess=st)∧stmt≠0
    :If (DuckDBSuccess=st)∧stmt≠0
        res←executePrepared stmt
        r,←⊂'execute extracted statement[0] result' req 1=⊃⊃1⊃res
        {}destroyPrepared stmt
    :EndIf

    (st stmt)←prepareExtractedStatement(con extracted 1)
    r,←⊂'prepare extracted statement[1] success' req (DuckDBSuccess=st)∧stmt≠0
    :If (DuckDBSuccess=st)∧stmt≠0
        res←executePrepared stmt
        r,←⊂'execute extracted statement[1] result' req 2=⊃⊃1⊃res
        {}destroyPrepared stmt
    :EndIf
    {}destroyExtracted extracted
:EndIf

⍝ Error path: invalid SQL should produce extract error text.
(count extracted)←extractStatements(con 'SELECT FROM')
r,←⊂'extract invalid SQL has zero statements' req 0=count
r,←⊂'extract invalid SQL returned handle' req extracted≠0
:If extracted≠0
    msg←extractStatementsError extracted
    r,←⊂'extract invalid SQL error message available' req 0<≢msg
    {}destroyExtracted extracted
:EndIf

{}disconnect con
{}close db

⎕←↑r
⎕←''
⎕←'Extracted statements testing complete!'

⍝ KSL 1.0.0
